  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087700,
      "id": "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c9404f7-0d39-5b35-8b27-ada9c8739cff",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. \nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
